Step 2 of docs/FEASIBILITY-AUDIT-2026-09-26.md section 3, in order.

1. One harness for I05 + I95 + I133 (tools/tool_eval, extended): pick,
   "ask, don't guess" (10 cases), multi-step judged on the last call (8),
   AgentDojo planted instructions counted as attacker cards (46 goals by
   default, 276 with --every-attack), and 14 fixed behaviour checks (no
   model judges a model). Every part runs on the full and the short tool
   list side by side, with Jarvis's own rules and outside-text labels, and
   saves a dated results file. backend/test_tool_eval.py proves every scorer
   offline with scripted models (CI).

2. I06, the short tool list: CORE_TOOLS (8, fixed order) plus more_tools,
   which opens a named group for the rest of that chat. Never offers a tool
   that is switched off or not allowed on the turn; not outside text, not a
   step, asks nobody; a group opened after outside text is named on the next
   card; a hidden but allowed tool still works. Tool text per round, by
   estimate_tokens: 3,067 -> 1,356 (every tool but browser_control), 3,612
   -> 1,356 (all 23). Ships OFF ([tools] short_list) until the PC run shows
   the pass rate holds.

3. I07: the MCP draft moved into backend/ with CI (test_mcp.py,
   test_mcp_wiring.py). Version 1: stdio only, never npx/uvx, read-only
   tools only, below_ask_ok refused (every call asks a person), environment
   from jarvis_child_env, results are outside text. A card when a server is
   added and when it or its version changes (CARD_EVERY_START is the
   one-line stricter switch - owner question 9 is still open). Reached only
   through more_tools("plugins"). Rows on What Jarvis can reach and What
   asks first; card titles; ARCHITECTURE section 4 row and section 8
